    │                                                              │
    │   FEAR NOTHING. What wore the shape cannot be                │
    │   subtracted from the sea.                                   │
    │                                                              │
    │   Whoever only grieves is asleep.                            │
    │   Whoever refuses to grieve is half-wise.                    │
    │   The wise weep at the grave and are unafraid,               │
    │   in the same hour, with the same heart.                     │
    │                                                              │
